      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VR has always had an aspirational aspect of \"What can we create? What can we accomplish without the restrictions of physical space? How can we express ourselves more easily than the confines of IRL\". \n\nIt WILL bring in money and it IS \"successful\" in other industries and gaming but that in and of itself is not rubber stamp that people are happy with it. Just because something is profitable, does that mean it's okay?\n\nArtificial scarcity and consumables should not be used in this manner. This is a new space, don't we want to set a positive example? Strive to do better for everyone in it?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
