      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The new Christmas items in VRChat are cool, but the Portable Winterizer is not. A paid consumable item is a predatory, FOMO-based monetization strategy and is a major step in the wrong direction. While I understand that VRChat needs to generate a profit, it should also respect its user base. \n\nPaying real money for a virtual item that lasts only three minutes and provides just five charges, only to have it disappear afterward and require a repurchase, sounds absolutely ridiculous. It’s one thing if the virtual item has some lasting value or is part of a long-term progression system, but paying real money for something that’s basically disposable after a few minutes or charges seems pretty exploitative. Paid consumable items are nonsensical, especially on a social VR platform. \n\nVRChat consistently makes some of the most questionable decisions imaginable.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
